WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.438 --> 00:00:05.863
Careful. now. This is why we came in early...

2
00:00:05.963 --> 00:00:08.890
so we can get it right before your inspection.

3
00:00:08.989 --> 00:00:10.519
And I really appreciate it.

4
00:00:10.652 --> 00:00:12.913
- Master Sergeant. - Don't kiss my ass.

5
00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:14.909
Just get it right.

6
00:00:14.975 --> 00:00:18.468
Now. remember your breath.

7
00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:20.895
Don't tense up.

8
00:00:20.961 --> 00:00:24.354
But don't be too loose either.

9
00:00:25.584 --> 00:00:27.278
Firm. but gentle.

10
00:00:27.412 --> 00:00:29.142
Like you're petting a baby kitten.

11
00:00:32.601 --> 00:00:34.364
Guess you didn't grow up with kittens.

12
00:00:34.431 --> 00:00:36.059
I had a turtle.

13
00:00:36.159 --> 00:00:37.256
Well. go on.

14
00:00:37.357 --> 00:00:39.119
Fuse is not gonna collect itself.

15
00:00:39.219 --> 00:00:41.746
If that was live. we'd be lights-out.

16
00:00:41.846 --> 00:00:45.405
I know. Master Sergeant. and I really appreciate the...

17
00:00:45.505 --> 00:00:47.200
Are you kidding me. private?

18
00:00:47.301 --> 00:00:48.962
Literally everything

19
00:00:49.062 --> 00:00:51.191
in this room was designed to kill you.

20
00:00:51.291 --> 00:00:53.785
I swear you'd lose your ass if it wasn't attached.

21
00:00:53.885 --> 00:00:55.647
Sorry.

22
00:01:00.535 --> 00:01:03.728
Well. is there a problem. private?

23
00:01:35.454 --> 00:01:38.447
All right. all right. Relax. relax. Take a deep breath.

24
00:01:38.547 --> 00:01:41.107
Let me. uh. let me see what I can find out.

25
00:01:41.208 --> 00:01:43.069
Any of you hearing any chatter?

26
00:01:43.136 --> 00:01:45.132
Uh. can you be a little more specific?

27
00:01:45.231 --> 00:01:48.091
Yeah. 'cause if it's about the omelet bar in the cafeteria.

28
00:01:48.224 --> 00:01:50.086
I think we can finally let that dream die.

29
00:01:50.187 --> 00:01:53.213
No. no. not breakfast. Army CID.

30
00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:55.441
You mean. NCIS in camo?

31
00:01:55.574 --> 00:01:57.602
Those guys. Last time we had a joint case with the Army.

32
00:01:57.735 --> 00:01:59.332
it turned into a full-blown turf war.

33
00:01:59.432 --> 00:02:01.060
Yeah. I know. This is not about a case.

34
00:02:01.161 --> 00:02:02.823
They're facing a RIF.

35
00:02:02.889 --> 00:02:04.520
Reduction in force?

36
00:02:04.619 --> 00:02:05.816
Rumor is...

37
00:02:05.915 --> 00:02:07.379
they're shutting down the whole agency.

38
00:02:07.513 --> 00:02:09.641
The entire Criminal Investigative Division?

39
00:02:09.740 --> 00:02:11.835
- Says who? - I got my sources.

40
00:02:11.935 --> 00:02:13.532
It's the whole agency we're talking about here.

41
00:02:13.631 --> 00:02:16.093
Like. thousands of jobs and cases. I'm sure.

42
00:02:16.193 --> 00:02:17.888
if this was real. Vance would've said something.

43
00:02:17.988 --> 00:02:20.782
Yeah. assuming Vance is still saying anything to anyone.

44
00:02:20.846 --> 00:02:21.944
I've barely seen him lately.

45
00:02:22.045 --> 00:02:23.541
Yeah. rumor has it that

46
00:02:23.675 --> 00:02:25.504
the Army CID is shutting down.

47
00:02:25.603 --> 00:02:27.599
And handing their caseload to us.

48
00:02:27.666 --> 00:02:30.858
Wait. NCIS is picking up CID's slack?

49
00:02:30.958 --> 00:02:32.520
So you have heard something?

50
00:02:32.654 --> 00:02:33.951
Same whispers. yeah.

51
00:02:34.051 --> 00:02:35.580
But I've been around long enough to know

52
00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:37.309
that rumors are like mold.

53
00:02:37.409 --> 00:02:39.538
You give them oxygen. they spread.

54
00:02:40.867 --> 00:02:44.028
Good morning. We're looking for Special Agent Jessica Knight.

55
00:02:44.925 --> 00:02:46.621
Okay. Who's asking?

56
00:02:46.721 --> 00:02:48.151
Army Criminal Investigative Division. ma'am.

57
00:02:48.284 --> 00:02:50.678
Your assistance has been requested at Fort Belvoir.

58
00:02:50.777 --> 00:02:51.909
Urgent situation.

59
00:02:51.975 --> 00:02:53.471
What kind of situation?

60
00:02:53.571 --> 00:02:54.868
We're not at liberty to say.

61
00:02:54.935 --> 00:02:56.631
but you'll be read in once you get there.

62
00:02:57.795 --> 00:02:59.258
I guess you'd better go.

63
00:02:59.392 --> 00:03:02.086
Keep us posted.

64
00:03:03.382 --> 00:03:06.774
CID's already asking for help with their cases?

65
00:03:06.907 --> 00:03:08.404
This mean the rumors are true?

66
00:03:09.368 --> 00:03:12.726
Not sure. but I think I know why they want Knight.

67
00:03:12.826 --> 00:03:15.920
"Standoff at Fort Belvoir."

68
00:03:18.248 --> 00:03:20.774
Remember. be the arrow.

69
00:03:20.874 --> 00:03:23.269
Y'all are the tip. shaft. and fletching. I'm the bow.

70
00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:26.760
And on my command. we fly.

71
00:03:29.222 --> 00:03:31.018
- Go. - Major Malone?

72
00:03:31.151 --> 00:03:34.310
NCIS Special Agent Knight. Hear you're looking for me.

73
00:03:34.410 --> 00:03:37.667
Agent Knight. Glad you could join us. Let's get to work.

74
00:03:37.801 --> 00:03:39.099
Still waiting on a sitrep.

75
00:03:39.198 --> 00:03:40.695
Male suspect. Clearly agitated.

76
00:03:40.793 --> 00:03:43.321
Held two men at gunpoint in the ammo warehouse.

77
00:03:43.422 --> 00:03:46.448
Let them go and barricaded himself inside.

78
00:03:46.547 --> 00:03:48.477
Then I'm gonna need a phone with a recorded line.

79
00:03:48.609 --> 00:03:52.135
warehouse schematics. and. uh. eyes on any surveillance feeds.

80
00:03:53.132 --> 00:03:54.628
Is there a problem?

81
00:03:54.728 --> 00:03:57.123
Oh. I'd call it more of a misunderstanding. Agent Knight.

82
00:03:57.223 --> 00:03:59.651
Well. my understanding is that I'm here for a reason.

83
00:03:59.783 --> 00:04:01.048
I'm a trained negotiator.

84
00:04:01.114 --> 00:04:03.176
Well. you were brought here for a reason.

85
00:04:03.275 --> 00:04:04.805
Just not that one.

86
00:04:04.939 --> 00:04:06.767
Negotiations are my job.

87
00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:08.863
So. what then... am I here for the snacks?

88
00:04:08.962 --> 00:04:12.088
Almost. Well. you are the snack.

89
00:04:12.187 --> 00:04:13.351
Come again?

90
00:04:13.451 --> 00:04:17.243
Some suspects ask for pizza or burgers.

91
00:04:17.342 --> 00:04:18.739
But this guy is sitting

92
00:04:18.839 --> 00:04:20.502
on enough munitions to level a city block.

93
00:04:20.568 --> 00:04:22.663
and he only made one request.

94
00:04:23.828 --> 00:04:24.725
You.

95
00:04:24.826 --> 00:04:26.222
Did he say why?

96
00:04:26.322 --> 00:04:29.048
Claims he's your little brother.

97
00:04:39.657 --> 00:04:41.319
- Delta. stand by. - Yes. sir.

98
00:04:41.453 --> 00:04:42.516
Okay.

99
00:04:42.616 --> 00:04:44.779
So. you don't have a little brother.

100
00:04:44.845 --> 00:04:46.874
Uh. no. Just an older brother in Houston

101
00:04:46.974 --> 00:04:49.101
and a younger sister that lives at an ashram in India.

102
00:04:49.168 --> 00:04:52.893
Well. this guy was very insistent. so if he's not

103
00:04:52.993 --> 00:04:55.088
a relative. who the hell is he?

104
00:04:55.154 --> 00:04:57.382
There's only one way to find out.

105
00:04:57.449 --> 00:04:59.544
Hold up.

106
00:04:59.643 --> 00:05:02.804
We still don't know who this guy is or what his endgame is.

107
00:05:02.936 --> 00:05:05.031
But he's agitated. disoriented.

108
00:05:05.131 --> 00:05:07.126
You're walking in cold.

109
00:05:07.226 --> 00:05:09.354
So I need to be crystal clear about protocol.

110
00:05:09.454 --> 00:05:12.813
I'm not here to freelance. I'm here to make contact.

111
00:05:12.913 --> 00:05:16.371
Well. I get that. But in this tent.

112
00:05:16.437 --> 00:05:18.732
I'm Fred. you're Ginger.

113
00:05:19.631 --> 00:05:22.025
I lead. You follow.

114
00:05:22.091 --> 00:05:23.355
Oh.

115
00:05:24.585 --> 00:05:27.212
Well. then just don't step on my toes.

116
00:05:33.698 --> 00:05:36.225
This better be Agent Knight.

117
00:05:36.325 --> 00:05:37.488
It is.

118
00:05:37.589 --> 00:05:39.783
Now I need to know who I'm speaking to.

119
00:05:39.883 --> 00:05:43.042
Jess? Uh...

120
00:05:43.142 --> 00:05:45.604
It's. um. it's me.

121
00:05:45.670 --> 00:05:48.429
Ryan. Uh. Ryan Harper.

122
00:05:48.529 --> 00:05:50.824
Ryan Harper?

123
00:05:50.924 --> 00:05:52.520
My old informant?

124
00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:53.884
Yeah.

125
00:05:53.984 --> 00:05:55.646
You remember what you used to call me?

126
00:05:55.746 --> 00:05:58.607
"Little brother." Your code name.

127
00:05:58.706 --> 00:06:01.366
-We took down that drug ring -Yeah. and you got me out.

128
00:06:01.466 --> 00:06:04.425
You know. you said I deserved a shot at something better.

129
00:06:04.526 --> 00:06:05.956
Yeah. so you joined the Army.

130
00:06:06.089 --> 00:06:08.383
You know. this is a pretty big production. uh.

131
00:06:08.450 --> 00:06:09.447
just to get in touch with me.

132
00:06:09.581 --> 00:06:11.942
Uh... Yeah. well. I. uh.

133
00:06:12.042 --> 00:06:15.300
I tried calling your cell. but I guess you changed

134
00:06:15.433 --> 00:06:17.063
your number. so. uh.

135
00:06:17.162 --> 00:06:19.258
I just. uh... Look. uh.

136
00:06:19.357 --> 00:06:21.486
I just. I really...

137
00:06:21.586 --> 00:06:24.179
I really need someone that I can trust right now.

138
00:06:24.279 --> 00:06:25.975
So. how about you start by telling me

139
00:06:26.075 --> 00:06:27.606
what the hell is going on.

140
00:06:27.705 --> 00:06:30.665
'Cause the guy I knew risked his life to wear a wire.

141
00:06:30.731 --> 00:06:32.560
not to hold a warehouse hostage.

142
00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:34.789
I... I don't want to hurt anyone.

143
00:06:34.888 --> 00:06:37.348
You know? I just... I thought this place would be empty.

144
00:06:37.415 --> 00:06:38.380
You know? Somewhere I could just

145
00:06:38.480 --> 00:06:40.176
go and-and clear my head.

146
00:06:40.275 --> 00:06:42.370
And then those two soldiers came.

147
00:06:42.504 --> 00:06:44.332
and-and I-and I-and I pulled my gun.

148
00:06:44.398 --> 00:06:45.929
And-and...

149
00:06:46.028 --> 00:06:47.525
It was a mistake.

150
00:06:47.625 --> 00:06:49.720
It was-it was a stupid. stupid mistake.

151
00:06:49.820 --> 00:06:51.649
And you let them go. That was good.

152
00:06:51.748 --> 00:06:53.412
Yeah. but then the MPs showed up

153
00:06:53.511 --> 00:06:55.972
and CID right after them. which is bad.

154
00:06:56.837 --> 00:06:58.167
So why is that bad?

155
00:06:58.299 --> 00:07:00.262
What happened right before you got to the warehouse?

156
00:07:00.328 --> 00:07:03.721
No! No. No. not-not with CID listening.

157
00:07:03.821 --> 00:07:06.979
I-I can't trust them. I can't trust anyone but you.

158
00:07:08.975 --> 00:07:10.472
Then come out and we will talk.

159
00:07:10.571 --> 00:07:13.564
I-I can't do that. No. you have to come in.

160
00:07:13.631 --> 00:07:16.724
And turn a standoff into a hostage situation?

161
00:07:16.823 --> 00:07:17.721
Not happening.

162
00:07:22.310 --> 00:07:24.605
Okay. how about we not take out our frustrations

163
00:07:24.705 --> 00:07:27.232
- on things that go boom. - I am trying. Jess.

164
00:07:27.298 --> 00:07:29.893
I am. but it's just. uh.

165
00:07:29.992 --> 00:07:32.753
it's all messed-up. I-I need help.

166
00:07:32.885 --> 00:07:34.183
And I'm here to help you.

167
00:07:34.249 --> 00:07:36.478
So. please. just calm down and talk to me.

168
00:07:36.578 --> 00:07:39.071
You say you trust me? Prove it.

169
00:07:39.171 --> 00:07:41.898
Go-go see Evelyn first. then call me back.

170
00:07:43.228 --> 00:07:44.392
Who's Evelyn?

171
00:07:44.526 --> 00:07:47.320
That's his mother. She lives in Suffolk.

172
00:07:47.385 --> 00:07:49.680
I can have an NCIS team at her house in 20 minutes.

173
00:07:49.779 --> 00:07:50.877
Maybe she'll tell us something.

174
00:07:51.010 --> 00:07:52.607
Uh. I doubt that.

175
00:07:52.707 --> 00:07:55.233
According to Sergeant Harper's files.

176
00:07:55.334 --> 00:07:58.027
his mother died last October.

177
00:07:58.127 --> 00:07:59.491
If your pal

178
00:07:59.557 --> 00:08:01.287
doesn't stop throwing around high-grade ordnance

179
00:08:01.353 --> 00:08:03.547
and asking for dead relatives.

180
00:08:03.681 --> 00:08:06.375
we may have to end this the hard way.

181
00:08:16.983 --> 00:08:19.809
Okay. Alpha. head to high ground.

182
00:08:19.909 --> 00:08:23.002
Major Malone. I think we should slow our roll here.

183
00:08:23.135 --> 00:08:25.130
We don't have a roll.

184
00:08:25.231 --> 00:08:28.324
I have a disturbed suspect in a room full of munitions.

185
00:08:28.423 --> 00:08:31.616
Sergeant Harper isn't trying to hurt anyone. Let me try

186
00:08:31.715 --> 00:08:33.777
and figure out why he is in full meltdown.

187
00:08:33.876 --> 00:08:35.507
Who is he to you?

188
00:08:35.606 --> 00:08:38.267
I told you. A former CI.

189
00:08:38.366 --> 00:08:41.957
I never had a CI request me by name at a standoff.

190
00:08:43.055 --> 00:08:44.386
Seven years ago.

191
00:08:44.486 --> 00:08:47.045
Harper put himself in danger to do the right thing.

192
00:08:47.112 --> 00:08:50.338
Ten months wearing a wire. his life on the line every day.

193
00:08:50.405 --> 00:08:51.669
and he only got through that

194
00:08:51.769 --> 00:08:54.927
because he trusted me to have his back.

195
00:08:55.027 --> 00:08:57.123
And I owe him the same thing now.

196
00:08:57.954 --> 00:08:59.750
I don't have that luxury.

197
00:08:59.882 --> 00:09:02.975
To me. he's a loose flame in a powder keg.

198
00:09:06.068 --> 00:09:09.028
Harper mentioned his mother. We need to follow up on that.

199
00:09:09.161 --> 00:09:11.190
It could be the key to getting him out alive.

200
00:09:11.289 --> 00:09:13.817
Look. you are welcome to wait by the phone

201
00:09:13.883 --> 00:09:16.477
in case he says something useful.

202
00:09:16.577 --> 00:09:18.340
But I've got a job to do.

203
00:09:18.472 --> 00:09:21.000
Your lead. Fred.

204
00:09:21.898 --> 00:09:23.328
Mm.

205
00:09:26.155 --> 00:09:27.651
Sniper moving into position.

206
00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:29.481
Copy that. Tac Team.

207
00:09:30.312 --> 00:09:34.236
McGee? I need a favor. fast.

208
00:09:34.335 --> 00:09:35.732
Evelyn Harper.

209
00:09:35.831 --> 00:09:37.993
This was her place. Title's in her son's name now.

210
00:09:38.127 --> 00:09:41.286
Doesn't look like anyone's lived here for a while.

211
00:09:41.386 --> 00:09:43.880
Oh. Harper probably lives on base.

212
00:09:45.310 --> 00:09:47.272
Yep. Enlisted at 19.

213
00:09:47.405 --> 00:09:49.866
Artillery specialist. Two tours.

214
00:09:49.965 --> 00:09:51.363
So he knows explosives.

215
00:10:02.603 --> 00:10:04.465
- I kick. you go. - Yeah.

216
00:10:04.565 --> 00:10:05.729
NCIS!

217
00:10:13.710 --> 00:10:17.136
Appears we just swatted a pinball machine.

218
00:10:17.202 --> 00:10:18.666
Not just a pinball machine.

219
00:10:18.731 --> 00:10:21.160
a Ducati and a Jet Ski.

220
00:10:21.226 --> 00:10:23.853
We thinking Sergeant Harper won the Showcase Showdown here?

221
00:10:23.954 --> 00:10:26.846
Well. Price is Right doesn't shoot in Virginia. I've checked.

222
00:10:26.980 --> 00:10:30.040
How does an E-5 sergeant in the Army

223
00:10:30.172 --> 00:10:31.436
afford all this stuff?

224
00:10:31.536 --> 00:10:33.830
And why does he want Knight to find it?

225
00:10:35.260 --> 00:10:37.089
That stuff's not mine.

226
00:10:37.156 --> 00:10:40.248
Not on Army pay. it isn't. How'd you get it?

227
00:10:40.348 --> 00:10:43.308
That's the thing. Jess. I didn't get it.

228
00:10:44.139 --> 00:10:46.600
Is that why you wanted us to find it?

229
00:10:46.700 --> 00:10:48.097
You think someone planted it?

230
00:10:48.163 --> 00:10:49.993
It is much bigger than that. all right?

231
00:10:50.093 --> 00:10:51.389
No one's gonna believe me.

232
00:10:51.454 --> 00:10:53.351
I believe you. That's why you called me. right?

233
00:10:53.450 --> 00:10:55.081
That's why you sent me to the house.

234
00:10:55.181 --> 00:10:58.140
It doesn't end at the house. all right? They're gonna f...

235
00:10:58.239 --> 00:10:59.570
Oh. they're gonna f-find...

236
00:10:59.636 --> 00:11:01.432
Ryan. what are they gonna find?

237
00:11:01.531 --> 00:11:03.195
Someone's using me!

238
00:11:03.295 --> 00:11:05.755
Ryan. tell me what is going on.

239
00:11:07.917 --> 00:11:09.912
I'm so sorry I dragged you into this.

240
00:11:13.770 --> 00:11:15.732
Don't bother.

241
00:11:15.866 --> 00:11:17.828
He's on the verge of opening up. He just got spooked.

242
00:11:17.928 --> 00:11:19.224
I can feel it.

243
00:11:19.324 --> 00:11:21.485
Yeah. for good reason.

244
00:11:21.552 --> 00:11:23.713
It's not about toys in a garage.

245
00:11:25.210 --> 00:11:26.773
It's about murder.

246
00:11:26.873 --> 00:11:29.966
My team just searched your pal's apartment.

247
00:11:30.065 --> 00:11:33.890
Found a body. Killed with Sergeant Harper's own blade.

248
00:11:38.346 --> 00:11:41.572
Let me call him back. I can get him out of that warehouse.

249
00:11:41.671 --> 00:11:43.201
Do you see what he's doing?

250
00:11:43.334 --> 00:11:45.263
Those aren't the actions of a guy

251
00:11:45.329 --> 00:11:46.526
who's planning on coming out.

252
00:11:46.660 --> 00:11:48.955
He is spiraling. and you know it.

253
00:11:49.021 --> 00:11:50.484
Command. this is Alpha.

254
00:11:50.617 --> 00:11:52.380
Got visual on the suspect.

255
00:11:54.109 --> 00:11:55.074
Transmit feed.

256
00:11:55.141 --> 00:11:57.401
Suspect picked up a device.

257
00:11:57.501 --> 00:11:59.962
Could be a detonator.

258
00:12:00.062 --> 00:12:03.122
It could be a stress ball. You don't know.

259
00:12:04.219 --> 00:12:05.682
Alpha. do you have a shot?

260
00:12:05.782 --> 00:12:07.046
Hold on.

261
00:12:07.145 --> 00:12:08.941
Target acquired. Standing by.

262
00:12:09.074 --> 00:12:10.504
Let me get him back on the phone.

263
00:12:10.604 --> 00:12:12.233
And let him move out of sight?

264
00:12:12.333 --> 00:12:14.062
No. this could be our only shot.

265
00:12:14.162 --> 00:12:16.923
Suspect is assembling an explosive device.

266
00:12:17.754 --> 00:12:19.416
Please. just give me a chance.

267
00:12:19.516 --> 00:12:21.745
I can't leave this to chance.

268
00:12:22.576 --> 00:12:25.203
- Alpha. this is Command. - Major Malone. don't.

269
00:12:25.270 --> 00:12:26.500
No.

270
00:12:26.600 --> 00:12:28.064
- Send it. - Major Malo...

271
00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:31.090
Sent.

272
00:12:31.222 --> 00:12:34.781
Target down. I repeat: target down.

273
00:12:41.432 --> 00:12:42.829
Any word on Knight?

274
00:12:42.929 --> 00:12:45.323
She's on her way back from Fort Belvoir.

275
00:12:45.423 --> 00:12:46.486
and she's pissed.

276
00:12:46.587 --> 00:12:48.150
Of course she is. Her friend just

277
00:12:48.282 --> 00:12:50.477
took a bullet to the chest from a CID sniper.

278
00:12:50.611 --> 00:12:51.974
Yeah. miracle he survived.

279
00:12:52.107 --> 00:12:53.205
He's not out of the woods.

280
00:12:53.304 --> 00:12:54.501
He's still on life support.

281
00:12:54.602 --> 00:12:56.131
Did Knight ever get him to explain

282
00:12:56.263 --> 00:12:57.494
why he barricaded himself?

283
00:12:57.595 --> 00:12:59.989
Nope. CID is telling the story now.

284
00:13:00.089 --> 00:13:03.314
Public statement suggests that Harper murdered a soldier

285
00:13:03.414 --> 00:13:05.376
and then tried suicide by cop.

286
00:13:05.442 --> 00:13:09.101
CID also thought that Harper had a detonator in his hand.

287
00:13:09.233 --> 00:13:12.260
Turns out it was a training fuse from a practice session.

288
00:13:12.360 --> 00:13:14.588
So. yeah. not exactly buying CID's version.

289
00:13:14.688 --> 00:13:16.916
How you doing. Jess?

290
00:13:17.847 --> 00:13:20.008
I'm fine. Harper's not.

291
00:13:20.075 --> 00:13:21.605
CID got this wrong.

292
00:13:21.705 --> 00:13:23.434
I don't know. I mean. if

293
00:13:23.534 --> 00:13:26.859
somebody found a dead guy in my apartment with my sword

294
00:13:26.959 --> 00:13:29.386
in his chest. and I barricaded myself

295
00:13:29.487 --> 00:13:31.815
- in a room full of explosives... - Yeah.

296
00:13:31.914 --> 00:13:33.743
It looks bad.

297
00:13:33.843 --> 00:13:35.107
But Harper called me.

298
00:13:35.207 --> 00:13:37.434
Told me he was being used. and I believe him.

299
00:13:37.535 --> 00:13:40.028
Except that's all he said.

300
00:13:40.128 --> 00:13:41.258
And now it's CID's case.

301
00:13:41.358 --> 00:13:43.021
It's up to them to find the truth.

302
00:13:43.121 --> 00:13:45.216
I'm not sure Malone's interested in the truth.

303
00:13:45.316 --> 00:13:47.778
He had Harper pegged as a lost cause from the beginning.

304
00:13:47.843 --> 00:13:50.172
And with CID facing shutdown rumors.

305
00:13:50.271 --> 00:13:51.868
they need a clean win. not a messy headline.

306
00:13:51.968 --> 00:13:54.128
Point is. Harper isn't getting a fair shake.

307
00:13:54.228 --> 00:13:56.024
We are missing a piece of this puzzle.

308
00:13:56.158 --> 00:13:58.984
And you want to find it.

309
00:13:59.117 --> 00:14:01.745
Harper's not just an old informant.

310
00:14:01.811 --> 00:14:05.470
When I met him. I thought being a cop was kicking in doors

311
00:14:05.569 --> 00:14:07.664
and putting bad guys away.

312
00:14:07.797 --> 00:14:10.790
But Harper showed me that you could actually help people.

313
00:14:10.889 --> 00:14:13.018
He changed his life because of me.

314
00:14:13.118 --> 00:14:14.681
I didn't give up on him back then.

315
00:14:14.780 --> 00:14:17.009
and I'm not gonna give up on him now.

316
00:14:18.306 --> 00:14:20.068
Well. hypothetically.

317
00:14:20.167 --> 00:14:22.895
if we were to get involved here. how would we do it?

318
00:14:22.995 --> 00:14:24.192
Yeah. we have no body.

319
00:14:24.258 --> 00:14:26.187
- no evidence. - And no jurisdiction.

320
00:14:26.253 --> 00:14:28.483
It's CID's case. We'd be

321
00:14:28.582 --> 00:14:30.411
stepping on a lot of toes.

322
00:14:30.511 --> 00:14:32.173
Yeah. starting with Vance's.

323
00:14:32.239 --> 00:14:34.668
If he finds out we're double-dipping on CID...

324
00:14:34.768 --> 00:14:36.729
All valid points.

325
00:14:37.561 --> 00:14:38.824
So...

326
00:14:38.891 --> 00:14:41.552
let's go step on some toes.

327
00:14:43.647 --> 00:14:44.877
This isn't good. Parker.

328
00:14:45.010 --> 00:14:47.039
I'm getting a ton of calls from CID.

329
00:14:47.138 --> 00:14:49.500
How? Our investigation barely started.

330
00:14:49.599 --> 00:14:51.296
Oh. no. not calls about that.

331
00:14:51.362 --> 00:14:53.524
About the rumors of the CID shutdown.

332
00:14:53.624 --> 00:14:55.252
Folks are freaking out they're gonna lose their jobs.

333
00:14:55.353 --> 00:14:58.446
And I'm telling you now. I will not share a lab with Spike.

334
00:14:58.512 --> 00:15:00.008
Do I want to know who that is?

335
00:15:00.108 --> 00:15:02.702
Spike is the CID's version of me.

336
00:15:02.835 --> 00:15:05.994
except he keeps his lab at a crisp 58 degrees

337
00:15:06.094 --> 00:15:07.657
and plays jazz music all day long.

338
00:15:07.757 --> 00:15:08.954
What do you have against jazz?

339
00:15:09.020 --> 00:15:11.947
Oh. no. I'm not talking Miles Davis jazz

340
00:15:12.013 --> 00:15:13.378
or Coltrane jazz.

341
00:15:13.478 --> 00:15:16.137
I'm talking elevator music jazz.

342
00:15:16.271 --> 00:15:17.800
Hold music jazz.

343
00:15:17.900 --> 00:15:20.362
That's not jazz. That's a... that's a crime.

344
00:15:20.461 --> 00:15:21.791
And not the one I'm interested in.

345
00:15:21.923 --> 00:15:23.886
Right. Well. I may not have access

346
00:15:23.953 --> 00:15:26.413
to CID's evidence against Ryan Harper.

347
00:15:26.513 --> 00:15:28.542
but I do have access to his social media.

348
00:15:28.642 --> 00:15:30.902
and that tells a story all on its own.

349
00:15:30.969 --> 00:15:33.830
Specifically. about a dead guy in his living room.

350
00:15:33.929 --> 00:15:35.691
His name is Sergeant Joseph Yates.

351
00:15:35.791 --> 00:15:37.621
and he's all over Harper's socials.

352
00:15:37.753 --> 00:15:39.218
What's Valor House?

353
00:15:39.283 --> 00:15:42.276
Oh. Valor House is the charity that Yates and Harper

354
00:15:42.376 --> 00:15:45.170
started to help wounded veterans when they hit hard times.

355
00:15:45.269 --> 00:15:48.096
These guys put every minute of their lives into Valor House.

356
00:15:48.197 --> 00:15:49.593
Yeah. until Yates ended up with

357
00:15:49.726 --> 00:15:51.389
Harper's samurai sword in him.

358
00:15:51.489 --> 00:15:54.482
Technically. that evidence is still circumstantial. but again.

359
00:15:54.547 --> 00:15:56.510
my ability to dig is limited.

360
00:15:56.577 --> 00:15:58.406
There must be somebody that we can talk to.

361
00:15:58.505 --> 00:16:01.132
Thankfully. there is. Harper has a girlfriend.

362
00:16:01.232 --> 00:16:02.563
Amanda Adams.

363
00:16:02.662 --> 00:16:04.159
They've been dating for about three months.

364
00:16:04.225 --> 00:16:06.387
and she spent as much time with Harper as Yates did.

365
00:16:06.519 --> 00:16:08.250
In fact. the three of them all seemed pretty close.

366
00:16:08.349 --> 00:16:10.145
Amanda might be able to tell us more

367
00:16:10.211 --> 00:16:11.674
about what happened between these two.

368
00:16:11.774 --> 00:16:13.104
All right. send her info to Knight.

369
00:16:13.171 --> 00:16:15.532
and keep looking into this charity.

370
00:16:15.632 --> 00:16:17.428
As long as I can do it from my warm

371
00:16:17.494 --> 00:16:19.988
and jazz-free lab.

372
00:16:24.810 --> 00:16:26.573
Amanda?

373
00:16:26.672 --> 00:16:28.136
How's Ryan doing?

374
00:16:28.236 --> 00:16:32.060
Stable. they say. but the chaplain's still on standby.

375
00:16:32.160 --> 00:16:34.322
They have a lot of great doctors here.

376
00:16:34.454 --> 00:16:37.713
If you're with CID. I'm not answering any more questions.

377
00:16:37.780 --> 00:16:40.474
No. I'm not. I'm Jessica Knight.

378
00:16:40.574 --> 00:16:42.170
with NCIS.

379
00:16:46.094 --> 00:16:47.291
Jessica Knight. um...

380
00:16:47.424 --> 00:16:49.187
Ryan talked about you.

381
00:16:49.287 --> 00:16:52.247
Said you used to have Sunday dinners at his mom's.

382
00:16:52.379 --> 00:16:54.408
Yeah. We did.

383
00:16:54.507 --> 00:16:56.868
Also said that you were the reason he joined the Army.

384
00:16:56.967 --> 00:16:59.396
Said you inspired him to serve.

385
00:16:59.530 --> 00:17:00.892
Yeah.

386
00:17:01.027 --> 00:17:03.919
I should have kept in better touch with him.

387
00:17:04.717 --> 00:17:08.210
Amanda. I'm trying to figure out what led Ryan to that warehouse.

388
00:17:08.309 --> 00:17:11.035
Because the Ryan that I knew was thoughtful

389
00:17:11.168 --> 00:17:12.864
and level-headed.

390
00:17:12.965 --> 00:17:14.794
Everything was fine.

391
00:17:14.893 --> 00:17:16.390
until a few weeks ago.

392
00:17:16.490 --> 00:17:18.883
He noticed something weird with the charity's bank account.

393
00:17:18.985 --> 00:17:20.381
Weird how?

394
00:17:20.481 --> 00:17:23.041
Money was missing.

395
00:17:23.175 --> 00:17:25.270
From Valor House. Ryan couldn't figure out

396
00:17:25.369 --> 00:17:28.328
how it disappeared. He started obsessing.

397
00:17:28.428 --> 00:17:30.590
Well. it makes sense that he'd be concerned.

398
00:17:30.690 --> 00:17:33.483
It was more than concern. He got paranoid.

399
00:17:33.583 --> 00:17:36.344
First. about the money. then other things.

400
00:17:36.443 --> 00:17:38.405
Look...

401
00:17:38.472 --> 00:17:40.035
Ryan wasn't crazy.

402
00:17:41.066 --> 00:17:44.258
Yes. he was agitated. on edge. but

403
00:17:44.358 --> 00:17:45.721
that doesn't make him a killer.

404
00:17:45.821 --> 00:17:47.816
Of course not.

405
00:17:47.917 --> 00:17:50.311
Can I ask you about Sergeant Yates?

406
00:17:50.444 --> 00:17:52.273
Did he have access to the bank account?

407
00:17:52.406 --> 00:17:55.200
I don't know. They ran the charity together.

408
00:17:55.299 --> 00:17:58.657
Is it possible that Ryan confronted him about this?

409
00:17:58.757 --> 00:17:59.922
Things got heated?

410
00:18:00.022 --> 00:18:01.717
I told you. Ryan's not a murderer.

411
00:18:01.817 --> 00:18:03.181
If you knew him. you'd know that.

412
00:18:03.281 --> 00:18:05.409
- Amanda...

413
00:18:06.606 --> 00:18:08.103
I promise you

414
00:18:08.235 --> 00:18:11.295
that I will do everything that I can to find out the truth.

415
00:18:13.457 --> 00:18:16.250
So. girlfriend was right.

416
00:18:16.350 --> 00:18:18.212
Lot of money disappeared from the charity.

417
00:18:18.345 --> 00:18:21.371
Transferred to Bitcoin accounts? Good luck tracking that.

418
00:18:21.471 --> 00:18:23.001
Mm-hmm.

419
00:18:23.068 --> 00:18:25.163
I guess. if your best buddy was stealing from your charity.

420
00:18:25.262 --> 00:18:27.091
it might make you "stab with a sword" mad.

421
00:18:27.191 --> 00:18:29.054
Well. Harper's girlfriend said he was paranoid.

422
00:18:29.153 --> 00:18:31.481
- Confirms CID's theory. - Well. we have no idea

423
00:18:31.580 --> 00:18:33.044
what Harper and Yates were really up to.

424
00:18:33.144 --> 00:18:34.607
let alone a motive for murder.

425
00:18:34.707 --> 00:18:37.434
Think I found a video online here that might help.

426
00:18:37.533 --> 00:18:39.329
I crowdsourced social platforms

427
00:18:39.462 --> 00:18:42.822
looking for recent images of Harper or Yates.

428
00:18:42.954 --> 00:18:44.817
Came across this.

429
00:18:44.917 --> 00:18:46.845
Trail mix with pretzels.

430
00:18:46.945 --> 00:18:49.273
Um. are we watching the right video?

431
00:18:49.339 --> 00:18:52.067
Yup. From the user "TheCalmCamouflage."

432
00:18:52.167 --> 00:18:54.626
The guy posts Army-themed ASMR content.

433
00:18:54.761 --> 00:18:56.656
MSM. uh. what?

434
00:18:56.789 --> 00:18:58.418
Autonomous sensory meridian response.

435
00:18:58.517 --> 00:19:00.747
Audio stimuli that. uh. results

436
00:19:00.813 --> 00:19:03.274
in a tingling sensation in the back of the head. Whispering.

437
00:19:03.373 --> 00:19:04.738
- tapping. - All right.

438
00:19:04.803 --> 00:19:06.267
Ignore the guy on the microphone.

439
00:19:06.366 --> 00:19:08.229
Look who is behind him.

440
00:19:11.023 --> 00:19:12.086
Harper and Yates.

441
00:19:12.186 --> 00:19:13.849
Except all I hear is the wrapper.

442
00:19:13.949 --> 00:19:15.412
Yeah. we might not be able to hear them.

443
00:19:15.512 --> 00:19:17.573
but a couple years ago. I created

444
00:19:17.673 --> 00:19:19.935
a lip-reading program as a birthday present for Abby.

445
00:19:20.035 --> 00:19:22.229
That is an oddly specific present.

446
00:19:22.329 --> 00:19:24.856
Anyway. I ran this video through my program.

447
00:19:24.923 --> 00:19:26.586
Look what it came up with.

448
00:19:28.248 --> 00:19:30.609
Hey. I'm freaking out. I don't know what to do.

449
00:19:30.710 --> 00:19:33.204
It's okay. man. Hey. I got you.

450
00:19:33.336 --> 00:19:35.332
But this-this could blow back on me.

451
00:19:35.431 --> 00:19:37.826
I'm gonna talk to Matt.

452
00:19:37.893 --> 00:19:39.422
He'll handle everything.

453
00:19:39.522 --> 00:19:42.782
Unfortunately. that is where the wrapper-wrinkling ends.

454
00:19:42.848 --> 00:19:45.242
"Handle everything"? As in the missing money?

455
00:19:45.342 --> 00:19:46.505
Yeah. that's what it sounds like.

456
00:19:46.606 --> 00:19:47.870
Which means Harper wasn't

457
00:19:47.969 --> 00:19:49.565
accusing Yates of stealing the money.

458
00:19:49.666 --> 00:19:51.062
He was asking for help to find it.

459
00:19:51.162 --> 00:19:53.988
Help from Matt. Do we have any idea who that is?

460
00:19:54.088 --> 00:19:56.616
I do. I have Yates' cell records.

461
00:19:56.682 --> 00:19:58.378
How were you able to pull phone records?

462
00:19:58.477 --> 00:20:01.605
Courtesy of my contact at the phone company.

463
00:20:01.671 --> 00:20:02.835
The last call Yates made

464
00:20:02.934 --> 00:20:04.497
before he died was to a cell phone

465
00:20:04.598 --> 00:20:06.459
belonging to Matthew Malone.

466
00:20:06.559 --> 00:20:09.619
As in Army Major Malone from CID?

467
00:20:09.719 --> 00:20:13.011
Major Malone. who ordered his sniper to shoot Harper?

468
00:20:13.110 --> 00:20:15.139
- Yes and yes. - All right. let me get this straight.

469
00:20:15.272 --> 00:20:16.735
these two friends discover this

470
00:20:16.802 --> 00:20:18.431
stolen money and then they

471
00:20:18.531 --> 00:20:19.828
went to report it to CID?

472
00:20:19.928 --> 00:20:21.758
And the next day. one of them

473
00:20:21.857 --> 00:20:23.220
turns up dead. and the other one?

474
00:20:23.286 --> 00:20:25.515
- Shot by CID. - Well. makes you wonder

475
00:20:25.615 --> 00:20:27.078
if. uh. they discovered a crime

476
00:20:27.210 --> 00:20:29.572
that Malone didn't want anyone to look into.

477
00:20:29.705 --> 00:20:32.398
Harper didn't trust CID. He made that very clear.

478
00:20:32.499 --> 00:20:35.658
And before you could find out why. Malone shut him up.

479
00:20:35.758 --> 00:20:38.552
I think it's time we have a talk with Major Malone.

480
00:20:38.651 --> 00:20:39.749
-I think someone's gonna have to

481
00:20:39.881 --> 00:20:41.744
break the news to Vance.

482
00:20:41.844 --> 00:20:43.207
He may already know.

483
00:20:43.340 --> 00:20:46.566
Vance wants me and Knight in his office. now.

484
00:20:48.927 --> 00:20:51.554
I just got off the phone with the director of CID.

485
00:20:51.688 --> 00:20:54.780
Apparently. there's a secondary investigation underway.

486
00:20:54.880 --> 00:20:56.908
Something they thought I should be made aware of.

487
00:20:57.008 --> 00:20:59.070
And it involves your team.

488
00:20:59.901 --> 00:21:01.364
Well. we were coming here to loop you in.

489
00:21:01.465 --> 00:21:03.293
We've been following a lead.

490
00:21:03.393 --> 00:21:06.054
One that may involve a CID agent

491
00:21:06.153 --> 00:21:08.082
tied to a financial coverup.

492
00:21:08.149 --> 00:21:09.745
Specifically. Major Malone.

493
00:21:09.845 --> 00:21:11.307
Good to know.

494
00:21:11.442 --> 00:21:14.168
But that's not the investigation that I'm talking about.

495
00:21:14.267 --> 00:21:17.428
Does the name Roland Massi mean anything to you?

496
00:21:17.494 --> 00:21:21.218
He's the drug dealer that Harper helped take down. but

497
00:21:21.318 --> 00:21:24.644
Massi's serving 50 to life. so what's there to investigate?

498
00:21:24.743 --> 00:21:27.071
The investigation's not about him.

499
00:21:27.936 --> 00:21:29.565
It's about you. Agent Knight.

500
00:21:29.632 --> 00:21:31.528
I'm sorry. what?

501
00:21:31.594 --> 00:21:34.287
CID is placing you under review.

502
00:21:34.388 --> 00:21:36.848
Your security clearance has been suspended.

503
00:21:38.045 --> 00:21:40.440
Effective immediately.

504
00:21:49.486 --> 00:21:53.077
Roland Massi owned a series of bars and clubs

505
00:21:53.176 --> 00:21:55.305
across Virginia catering to service members.

506
00:21:55.372 --> 00:21:57.200
Served drinks in the front. cocaine in the back.

507
00:21:57.335 --> 00:21:59.396
It was one of the largest drug operations

508
00:21:59.495 --> 00:22:00.659
in the commonwealth's history.

509
00:22:00.759 --> 00:22:02.056
Until seven years ago.

510
00:22:02.155 --> 00:22:04.118
when the NCIS REACT team and I took it all down.

511
00:22:04.218 --> 00:22:06.613
Well. now Massi's serving life in prison.

512
00:22:06.712 --> 00:22:08.275
It's a big win for NCIS.

513
00:22:08.342 --> 00:22:10.935
None of this would have been possible without Ryan Harper.

514
00:22:11.002 --> 00:22:13.397
He was just a kid. He was seduced by Massi's offer

515
00:22:13.463 --> 00:22:16.256
of fast cash. realized it was plain wrong.

516
00:22:16.356 --> 00:22:18.949
So. he cooperated with Knight and turned his life around.

517
00:22:19.049 --> 00:22:21.942
Okay. but why would Malone be sniffing around

518
00:22:22.076 --> 00:22:23.772
a successful seven-year-old bust?

519
00:22:23.872 --> 00:22:26.699
Well. either he thinks Knight did something wrong...

520
00:22:26.798 --> 00:22:28.195
Or it's a bluff.

521
00:22:28.295 --> 00:22:29.791
To take our eyes off Malone and the missing money.

522
00:22:29.891 --> 00:22:32.053
Is there anything else about Massi's operation

523
00:22:32.118 --> 00:22:33.416
that we should know about?

524
00:22:33.516 --> 00:22:35.379
Everything you need to know is in that file.

525
00:22:35.445 --> 00:22:37.174
I stand by it.

526
00:22:38.339 --> 00:22:40.334
CID comes at one of ours.

527
00:22:40.400 --> 00:22:42.162
we don't wait around playing defense.

528
00:22:42.230 --> 00:22:43.991
We show them that this investigation

529
00:22:44.058 --> 00:22:45.256
isn't about Knight.

530
00:22:45.355 --> 00:22:47.483
it's about Malone. and we prove it

531
00:22:47.550 --> 00:22:48.979
before they bury the evidence.

532
00:22:49.046 --> 00:22:52.006
CID blindsided Knight the moment that we connected Malone

533
00:22:52.106 --> 00:22:54.700
with our victim. That is not a coincidence.

534
00:22:54.800 --> 00:22:56.861
This whole case revolves around

535
00:22:56.961 --> 00:22:58.691
that dead body in Harper's living room.

536
00:22:58.823 --> 00:23:00.586
All right. so we solve the murder.

537
00:23:00.686 --> 00:23:01.983
we hopefully clear Harper.

538
00:23:02.049 --> 00:23:04.111
and we definitely get CID off Knight's back.

539
00:23:04.211 --> 00:23:06.439
And. uh. someone needs to make sure

540
00:23:06.506 --> 00:23:09.266
that Vance stays off of ours.

541
00:23:09.332 --> 00:23:11.627
Yes. absolutely.

542
00:23:11.693 --> 00:23:13.656
Thank you.

543
00:23:15.352 --> 00:23:17.214
That was my third call with

544
00:23:17.348 --> 00:23:19.243
the CID director since breakfast.

545
00:23:19.343 --> 00:23:21.205
I'm not looking for a fourth.

546
00:23:21.304 --> 00:23:23.334
- That's the job. - Mine. yes.

547
00:23:23.433 --> 00:23:25.760
Right now. I'm more worried about Agent Knight's.

548
00:23:25.860 --> 00:23:27.324
Well. then we're on the same page.

549
00:23:27.424 --> 00:23:28.853
Are we?

550
00:23:29.651 --> 00:23:31.614
You said that you were investigating

551
00:23:31.714 --> 00:23:32.844
a CID agent.

552
00:23:32.976 --> 00:23:35.904
and now CID is digging into one of ours.

553
00:23:35.969 --> 00:23:38.498
The last thing that we need is a turf war.

554
00:23:38.598 --> 00:23:40.160
Because of the rumors they're folding.

555
00:23:40.260 --> 00:23:43.552
Yes. CID won't go down without a fight.

556
00:23:43.619 --> 00:23:45.614
They need a win. any way they can get it.

557
00:23:45.714 --> 00:23:46.645
Even at Knight's expense.

558
00:23:46.744 --> 00:23:48.807
CID is under the spotlight.

559
00:23:48.939 --> 00:23:50.968
and they need to get it off them fast.

560
00:23:51.102 --> 00:23:53.927
Taking down an NCIS agent... that's high-profile.

561
00:23:54.062 --> 00:23:55.923
Suddenly. the spotlight is on us.

562
00:23:56.023 --> 00:23:57.454
I don't care about the spotlight.

563
00:23:57.586 --> 00:23:59.183
I care that Knight's being used as a scapegoat.

564
00:23:59.250 --> 00:24:01.809
I wish it were that simple. Parker.

565
00:24:01.909 --> 00:24:03.904
But according to the CID director.

566
00:24:04.005 --> 00:24:06.732
whatever they have on Agent Knight is substantial.

567
00:24:06.831 --> 00:24:09.392
Major Malone is on his way over to interview her now.

568
00:24:10.389 --> 00:24:11.885
Okay. so how do we stop him?

569
00:24:12.020 --> 00:24:15.113
- We don't. He's within his rights. - So. what...

570
00:24:15.212 --> 00:24:16.974
we just let Knight take the hit?

571
00:24:17.074 --> 00:24:20.067
I said we can't stop Major Malone from questioning Knight.

572
00:24:20.201 --> 00:24:22.229
I never said that we were giving up.

573
00:24:23.526 --> 00:24:25.189
I'm trying to protect my agent.

574
00:24:25.322 --> 00:24:27.151
So am I.

575
00:24:27.250 --> 00:24:28.381
Which is why I made sure

576
00:24:28.514 --> 00:24:29.811
that Knight is being questioned here.

577
00:24:29.910 --> 00:24:31.873
on our turf. not theirs.

578
00:24:32.006 --> 00:24:33.702
And more importantly...

579
00:24:37.327 --> 00:24:39.455
...why I had CID hand over this.

580
00:24:42.581 --> 00:24:45.275
Crime scene report from Sergeant Harper's apartment?

581
00:24:46.273 --> 00:24:47.702
Thank you.

582
00:24:47.802 --> 00:24:49.000
Parker.

583
00:24:50.064 --> 00:24:51.960
If you're gonna prove that Harper's not a murderer.

584
00:24:52.059 --> 00:24:54.653
do it fast. But please be warned.

585
00:24:54.785 --> 00:24:57.247
CID is a drowning man.

586
00:24:58.045 --> 00:25:00.972
Drowning man doesn't care who he pulls under with him.

587
00:25:08.687 --> 00:25:09.618
Kasie?

588
00:25:11.713 --> 00:25:14.240
Uh. Kasie. you okay?

589
00:25:18.897 --> 00:25:20.027
Kasie?

590
00:25:20.127 --> 00:25:21.324
Wait. McGee. wait. watch out for the...

591
00:25:21.390 --> 00:25:23.985
paint.

592
00:25:24.084 --> 00:25:26.047
That's. uh. that's great.

593
00:25:26.147 --> 00:25:28.507
My shoes are now the same color as the squad room.

594
00:25:28.574 --> 00:25:30.402
Yeah. my forensic supplies are backordered.

595
00:25:30.536 --> 00:25:32.564
so I had to raid building maintenance.

596
00:25:32.664 --> 00:25:36.356
- Well. this place is a total mess. - Hey. You see a mess.

597
00:25:36.455 --> 00:25:38.052
but I see geometry.

598
00:25:38.184 --> 00:25:39.781
Because every slash

599
00:25:39.881 --> 00:25:42.740
and stab creates a mathematical pattern that tells a story.

600
00:25:42.841 --> 00:25:45.335
Yeah. a story with. uh. not a very happy ending.

601
00:25:45.467 --> 00:25:47.596
Mm. Depends on how you look at it.

602
00:25:47.696 --> 00:25:51.353
I am matching my demonstration to the crime scene photos from

603
00:25:51.487 --> 00:25:54.979
Sergeant Harper's apartment. and I finally got it right.

604
00:25:55.079 --> 00:25:56.875
What do you notice in these photos?

605
00:25:57.773 --> 00:25:58.936
Well. uh...

606
00:25:59.036 --> 00:26:00.899
Well. there's blood everywhere. I mean.

607
00:26:00.965 --> 00:26:02.494
it's on the floor. it's on the walls.

608
00:26:02.627 --> 00:26:05.122
- even the ceiling. - Ah. you almost got it right.

609
00:26:05.221 --> 00:26:07.283
Most of the blood is on half of the floor.

610
00:26:07.383 --> 00:26:08.947
the walls. the ceiling.

611
00:26:09.046 --> 00:26:10.642
Right. Murderer swings the sword.

612
00:26:10.776 --> 00:26:13.336
- blood spatters in the direction of the swing. - Exactly.

613
00:26:14.300 --> 00:26:16.894
I'm right-handed. so when I swing the sword.

614
00:26:16.961 --> 00:26:18.690
paint goes on the left side of the room.

615
00:26:18.757 --> 00:26:20.353
just like in the crime scene photos.

616
00:26:20.419 --> 00:26:21.982
Okay.

617
00:26:22.082 --> 00:26:24.277
Killer is right-handed. you are right-handed.

618
00:26:24.410 --> 00:26:27.270
- Mm-hmm. - As is 90% of the population.

619
00:26:28.600 --> 00:26:30.063
Unless Sergeant Harper is left-handed.

620
00:26:30.197 --> 00:26:32.093
Ding. ding. ding. Not only that.

621
00:26:32.192 --> 00:26:33.889
but judging by the angle of the swings.

622
00:26:33.988 --> 00:26:35.917
the killer was also significantly shorter

623
00:26:36.016 --> 00:26:37.081
than Harper as well.

624
00:26:37.181 --> 00:26:38.543
Harper didn't kill his friend.

625
00:26:38.644 --> 00:26:41.371
Bingo. CID's got the wrong man.

626
00:26:41.470 --> 00:26:42.967
- Ooh.

627
00:26:44.197 --> 00:26:45.561
It's Parker.

628
00:26:45.661 --> 00:26:47.489
Major Malone just got here to interrogate Knight.

629
00:26:47.556 --> 00:26:51.813
This evidence will show Malone how wrong he is about Harper.

630
00:26:53.942 --> 00:26:55.837
- Ladies first. - You're the guest.

631
00:26:55.937 --> 00:26:57.499
No. I insist.

632
00:26:57.599 --> 00:26:58.830
Hm.

633
00:27:05.581 --> 00:27:07.144
You got to be kidding me.

634
00:27:07.243 --> 00:27:08.574
Well. it's my interview.

635
00:27:08.641 --> 00:27:10.669
It's my interrogation room.

636
00:27:11.433 --> 00:27:13.296
How about a compromise?

637
00:27:13.429 --> 00:27:15.457
You got a pitch?

638
00:27:22.774 --> 00:27:24.636
I might as well start us off.

639
00:27:24.736 --> 00:27:26.299
Actually. you know what? I'll start.

640
00:27:26.431 --> 00:27:28.860
Ladies first. right?

641
00:27:30.222 --> 00:27:33.449
What the hell. I got nothing to hide.

642
00:27:33.582 --> 00:27:36.242
Mm. Except that you were the last person

643
00:27:36.342 --> 00:27:38.737
to speak to our murder victim.

644
00:27:39.535 --> 00:27:40.832
I didn't hide that.

645
00:27:40.898 --> 00:27:43.592
You didn't disclose it to me at the standoff.

646
00:27:43.725 --> 00:27:45.721
I had my hands full.

647
00:27:45.853 --> 00:27:47.416
And it wasn't your business.

648
00:27:47.550 --> 00:27:48.747
Oh.

649
00:27:48.879 --> 00:27:50.775
Sergeant Yates called about suspicious activity

650
00:27:50.875 --> 00:27:52.505
with the charity's accounts.

651
00:27:52.571 --> 00:27:54.633
We were gonna meet in the morning. but. uh.

652
00:27:54.733 --> 00:27:56.229
well. he's dead.

653
00:27:56.361 --> 00:27:59.189
So. you accused Harper of murdering him

654
00:27:59.288 --> 00:28:01.650
and had your sniper take him down.

655
00:28:01.749 --> 00:28:03.645
I stand by my actions.

656
00:28:03.712 --> 00:28:06.338
I believe Harper was a threat to himself and others.

657
00:28:06.472 --> 00:28:08.267
I made a judgment call.

658
00:28:08.367 --> 00:28:10.196
The wrong judgment call.

659
00:28:10.296 --> 00:28:12.159
Because Harper didn't kill that guy.

660
00:28:12.291 --> 00:28:14.020
He's innocent.

661
00:28:14.120 --> 00:28:18.078
Mm. you're half-right. He didn't kill the guy.

662
00:28:21.470 --> 00:28:22.568
You know?

663
00:28:22.667 --> 00:28:25.528
Sure. Harper's left-handed.

664
00:28:25.628 --> 00:28:26.957
The killer was right-handed.

665
00:28:27.090 --> 00:28:29.351
Which means you don't have a case.

666
00:28:29.452 --> 00:28:30.716
so what are we doing here?

667
00:28:30.781 --> 00:28:33.309
Harper didn't swing the sword but...

668
00:28:33.410 --> 00:28:34.971
oh. he was far from innocent.

669
00:28:35.105 --> 00:28:38.364
Now. while NCIS was playing gotcha with yesterday's clues.

670
00:28:38.431 --> 00:28:41.623
CID was actively pursuing fresh ones.

671
00:28:42.588 --> 00:28:44.783
Harper's tox report came back.

672
00:28:48.240 --> 00:28:50.302
He was hopped up on cocaine.

673
00:28:50.403 --> 00:28:52.730
which explains his erratic behavior yesterday.

674
00:28:53.528 --> 00:28:56.820
Explained even more when we searched his charity office.

675
00:28:56.920 --> 00:29:00.347
Found phones. drug-mixing paraphernalia.

676
00:29:00.412 --> 00:29:01.643
and...

677
00:29:03.738 --> 00:29:05.567
...six kilos of product.

678
00:29:05.667 --> 00:29:08.028
Your pal Harper wasn't just using.

679
00:29:08.161 --> 00:29:09.558
he was dealing.

680
00:29:09.690 --> 00:29:13.049
That missing charity money... he was laundering it.

681
00:29:13.182 --> 00:29:14.812
And when Yates found out.

682
00:29:14.912 --> 00:29:17.340
Harper had him killed.

683
00:29:17.440 --> 00:29:19.535
How is this even possible?

684
00:29:20.565 --> 00:29:23.159
I've been asking myself the same thing.

685
00:29:23.293 --> 00:29:26.618
I'd say you made it possible. Agent Knight.

686
00:29:27.416 --> 00:29:30.576
Ryan Harper never intended to go straight seven years ago.

687
00:29:30.642 --> 00:29:32.405
He was just biding his time.

688
00:29:32.504 --> 00:29:35.763
Harper was the reason we took down Roland Massi.

689
00:29:35.829 --> 00:29:38.922
Mm. sure. I mean. he was trying to survive.

690
00:29:38.989 --> 00:29:40.153
Oh.

691
00:29:41.317 --> 00:29:44.377
Harper helps you get rid of Massi.

692
00:29:44.443 --> 00:29:45.706
Then you expunge his record.

693
00:29:45.773 --> 00:29:47.768
which allowed him to join the Army.

694
00:29:48.733 --> 00:29:51.659
Where he builds a brand-new drug ring. all his own.

695
00:29:53.089 --> 00:29:54.586
This is ridiculous.

696
00:29:54.685 --> 00:29:56.249
Or are you so busy trying to prove

697
00:29:56.349 --> 00:29:58.244
how I screwed up. that...

698
00:29:58.377 --> 00:30:00.472
you can't even see your own mess?

699
00:30:01.569 --> 00:30:03.300
Even if you can't see it...

700
00:30:04.198 --> 00:30:05.893
...everyone else will.

701
00:30:06.990 --> 00:30:10.548
Now. this graduation photo is going on the cover of my report

702
00:30:10.682 --> 00:30:12.478
to the inspector general.

703
00:30:14.573 --> 00:30:18.564
Let's hope it doesn't make the cover of the Evening Post.

704
00:30:20.559 --> 00:30:22.122
Way I see it.

705
00:30:22.221 --> 00:30:25.912
you were either in on all this with Harper from the beginning

706
00:30:26.012 --> 00:30:27.543
or you got played.

707
00:30:27.642 --> 00:30:30.336
For me.

708
00:30:30.469 --> 00:30:33.096
I'd rather be a criminal than a fool.

709
00:30:37.154 --> 00:30:39.515
Knight has been there for a long time.

710
00:30:39.647 --> 00:30:41.543
Nobody's called for a medic yet.

711
00:30:41.643 --> 00:30:43.339
Is that good or bad?

712
00:30:44.204 --> 00:30:45.999
Hey. Knight.

713
00:30:46.100 --> 00:30:46.997
How'd it go in there?

714
00:30:47.097 --> 00:30:48.527
Uh. still sorting that out.

715
00:30:48.626 --> 00:30:52.119
You. uh. want to give us the headline?

716
00:30:53.482 --> 00:30:56.840
Actually. that's what I'm trying to avoid.

717
00:31:01.762 --> 00:31:04.390
Agent Knight. there something I can do for you?

718
00:31:05.620 --> 00:31:06.850
I got it wrong.

719
00:31:10.575 --> 00:31:12.039
If this is about the case.

720
00:31:12.105 --> 00:31:14.234
I'm sure it's something we can work out.

721
00:31:14.366 --> 00:31:16.063
Not this time.

722
00:31:17.027 --> 00:31:20.086
I thought I was making a difference in someone's life.

723
00:31:21.283 --> 00:31:23.179
But I just let myself get used.

724
00:31:23.279 --> 00:31:25.906
If CID wants to make themselves look good

725
00:31:26.039 --> 00:31:27.635
by taking me down. fine.

726
00:31:27.702 --> 00:31:31.160
but I won't let them take NCIS down with me.

727
00:31:31.260 --> 00:31:33.023
My mistake.

728
00:31:33.123 --> 00:31:35.118
I own it.

729
00:31:59.660 --> 00:32:00.891
Agent Parker.

730
00:32:01.688 --> 00:32:02.554
Can I help you?

731
00:32:02.686 --> 00:32:04.482
Called you twice. no answer.

732
00:32:04.549 --> 00:32:06.511
I'm aware.

733
00:32:06.611 --> 00:32:07.974
Convenient.

734
00:32:08.074 --> 00:32:10.136
Knight's resignation took the spotlight off NCIS.

735
00:32:10.203 --> 00:32:13.262
That's. uh. that's what you wanted.

736
00:32:14.027 --> 00:32:16.621
You think I wanted Agent Knight to resign?

737
00:32:17.818 --> 00:32:19.115
I think you let her.

738
00:32:19.215 --> 00:32:22.308
She didn't exactly invite a discussion.

739
00:32:22.374 --> 00:32:25.201
Now. if you'll excuse me. I have a call.

740
00:32:25.301 --> 00:32:27.329
She's being steamrolled. Leon. We can't

741
00:32:27.462 --> 00:32:28.992
just sit back and watch it happen.

742
00:32:29.092 --> 00:32:31.419
My hands are tied. Parker. What would you have me do?

743
00:32:31.486 --> 00:32:33.315
Well. you can start by blowing off your call

744
00:32:33.415 --> 00:32:35.444
and showing me you give a damn!

745
00:32:39.401 --> 00:32:42.827
Not every part of my job is up for public consumption.

746
00:32:43.624 --> 00:32:44.655
I'm the public now?

747
00:32:44.789 --> 00:32:47.715
Excuse me. Agent Parker.

748
00:32:55.397 --> 00:32:56.827
Parker. you're good?

749
00:32:56.927 --> 00:32:58.756
Any word from Knight since she left?

750
00:32:58.856 --> 00:33:00.585
Radio silence.

751
00:33:00.717 --> 00:33:01.882
Yeah.

752
00:33:01.982 --> 00:33:04.043
Major Malone is a major pain in the ass.

753
00:33:04.110 --> 00:33:06.073
- No argument here. - She made a call

754
00:33:06.172 --> 00:33:07.901
that any one of us would have made.

755
00:33:08.001 --> 00:33:10.528
Helping an informant expunge their record?

756
00:33:10.594 --> 00:33:12.025
Restorative justice 101.

757
00:33:12.124 --> 00:33:14.054
I wouldn't be standing here if someone

758
00:33:14.154 --> 00:33:16.314
didn't give me a second chance when I was 18.

759
00:33:16.381 --> 00:33:18.376
Right. but you became a cop.

760
00:33:18.476 --> 00:33:20.871
CID says that Harper became a drug lord.

761
00:33:20.971 --> 00:33:22.534
CID's evidence was enough

762
00:33:22.666 --> 00:33:24.362
to make Knight believe that she got played.

763
00:33:24.462 --> 00:33:25.859
And if it's true.

764
00:33:25.992 --> 00:33:29.019
that's not just a black mark. that's a career-ender.

765
00:33:29.119 --> 00:33:31.346
All right. but we all know Jessica Knight.

766
00:33:31.479 --> 00:33:33.541
Do we really think she got played?

767
00:33:34.772 --> 00:33:36.467
All right. if we're gonna save Knight. we need

768
00:33:36.534 --> 00:33:38.829
to tear down CID's case. find the holes.

769
00:33:38.929 --> 00:33:40.991
prove that Harper was no drug lord.

770
00:33:41.124 --> 00:33:42.520
Before CID goes public.

771
00:33:42.653 --> 00:33:44.050
Well. I've got something that may help.

772
00:33:44.149 --> 00:33:45.413
I've been reviewing the interview footage

773
00:33:45.480 --> 00:33:47.142
from Knight's interview with Malone.

774
00:33:47.242 --> 00:33:50.669
He may not have as much evidence as he claims. Take a look.

775
00:33:51.466 --> 00:33:53.029
Why is the table turned sideways?

776
00:33:53.128 --> 00:33:55.822
Neither of them would agree on who was interviewing who.

777
00:33:55.922 --> 00:33:57.153
Compromise?

778
00:33:57.253 --> 00:33:59.113
Or Knight knew we might want

779
00:33:59.213 --> 00:34:00.778
a view of Malone's files.

780
00:34:00.878 --> 00:34:02.641
including the drug analysis on the cocaine

781
00:34:02.773 --> 00:34:05.498
CID seized.

782
00:34:06.664 --> 00:34:09.058
- Bad analysis? - No. bad drugs.

783
00:34:09.125 --> 00:34:10.622
Compound contains

784
00:34:10.722 --> 00:34:12.915
less than 15% cocaine hydrochloride.

785
00:34:13.049 --> 00:34:15.776
Whereas street cocaine comes in about 60%.

786
00:34:15.876 --> 00:34:18.037
And about 90% for the pure stuff.

787
00:34:18.104 --> 00:34:19.567
Yeah. this was just enough to pop positive

788
00:34:19.701 --> 00:34:22.095
on a forensics analysis. The rest is baby laxatives.

789
00:34:22.194 --> 00:34:24.489
So Harper was trying to move faulty product?

790
00:34:25.253 --> 00:34:27.881
Or maybe he's not trying to move any product at all.

791
00:34:28.014 --> 00:34:30.041
It's an old cartel trick. They grab

792
00:34:30.142 --> 00:34:31.538
a small amount of the pure stuff.

793
00:34:31.639 --> 00:34:32.802
and you mix it with the junk

794
00:34:32.869 --> 00:34:33.867
to make it look like a large amount.

795
00:34:33.967 --> 00:34:34.931
and then they plant it.

796
00:34:35.031 --> 00:34:35.994
All right. who do we think

797
00:34:36.095 --> 00:34:37.191
Harper's being set up by?

798
00:34:37.292 --> 00:34:39.521
Bad cops plant drugs. too.

799
00:34:39.620 --> 00:34:41.781
You really think Malone would go that far?

800
00:34:41.882 --> 00:34:45.405
More than I believe. uh. Knight helped create a drug lord.

801
00:34:46.171 --> 00:34:48.534
All right. how do we prove it?

802
00:34:50.928 --> 00:34:52.590
Now. I'm not one to comment on

803
00:34:52.690 --> 00:34:54.951
interpersonal dynamics at work.

804
00:34:55.018 --> 00:34:57.412
- You're not? - Fine. I do it all the time.

805
00:34:57.479 --> 00:34:59.274
but some people need to be reminded

806
00:34:59.373 --> 00:35:01.269
that we're all team NCIS.

807
00:35:01.369 --> 00:35:03.897
and when friends argue. they need to hug.

808
00:35:03.997 --> 00:35:05.992
I'm not hugging Director Vance.

809
00:35:06.624 --> 00:35:07.589
Tell me you got something.

810
00:35:07.689 --> 00:35:09.350
Like holes in CID's case?

811
00:35:09.451 --> 00:35:12.643
Then you're in luck. because this major drug operation

812
00:35:12.777 --> 00:35:14.139
looks like Swiss cheese.

813
00:35:14.273 --> 00:35:17.232
For starters. the high-ticket items

814
00:35:17.299 --> 00:35:21.123
seized from the garage cost about $250.000.

815
00:35:21.222 --> 00:35:22.753
which is almost the exact amount

816
00:35:22.853 --> 00:35:24.615
- missing from Harper's charity. - Right. suggesting

817
00:35:24.749 --> 00:35:26.810
that the stolen charity money

818
00:35:26.909 --> 00:35:28.106
paid for the stuff. not drug money.

819
00:35:28.240 --> 00:35:31.166
Correct. Now. CID claims that

820
00:35:31.266 --> 00:35:33.261
the charity was being used to launder money.

821
00:35:33.395 --> 00:35:36.321
but that's impossible because there were no illicit funds

822
00:35:36.388 --> 00:35:37.519
being run through the charity.

823
00:35:37.619 --> 00:35:40.944
There are no drug sales at all.

824
00:35:41.043 --> 00:35:43.870
I ran the numbers from the burner phones that CID seized.

825
00:35:43.970 --> 00:35:45.832
They're full of coded messages

826
00:35:45.932 --> 00:35:47.927
that look like drug deals from The Wire.

827
00:35:48.027 --> 00:35:50.654
- Fake messages? - Uh. real messages.

828
00:35:50.754 --> 00:35:53.015
Fake deals. Someone used a bot program

829
00:35:53.115 --> 00:35:54.512
to make these phones call each other.

830
00:35:54.612 --> 00:35:58.037
So. no buyers. no profits. no operation.

831
00:35:58.136 --> 00:35:59.567
Just an elaborate frame job

832
00:35:59.667 --> 00:36:01.529
designed to fool CID and get Harper put away.

833
00:36:01.629 --> 00:36:03.923
Yeah. unless CID was in on it.

834
00:36:04.023 --> 00:36:07.282
Malone takes drugs from the evidence locker. plants them.

835
00:36:07.349 --> 00:36:10.408
There's no way that these drugs came from CID evidence locker.

836
00:36:10.508 --> 00:36:11.838
I ran the drug analysis

837
00:36:11.971 --> 00:36:14.166
through the DEA's database. They keep

838
00:36:14.265 --> 00:36:17.292
a index of all narcotics seized from all agencies.

839
00:36:17.426 --> 00:36:18.656
CID never seized

840
00:36:18.788 --> 00:36:21.317
this specific blend of cocaine.

841
00:36:21.417 --> 00:36:23.644
but NCIS did. seven years ago.

842
00:36:23.744 --> 00:36:25.772
When Knight took down Massi's organization.

843
00:36:25.906 --> 00:36:29.597
This compound was dealt exclusively by Massi's crew.

844
00:36:29.697 --> 00:36:31.924
until the entire operation

845
00:36:32.057 --> 00:36:33.588
was dismantled and the drugs were destroyed.

846
00:36:33.720 --> 00:36:35.915
Are you saying that somebody from Massi's organization

847
00:36:36.015 --> 00:36:38.277
are using seven-year-old drugs to frame Harper?

848
00:36:38.377 --> 00:36:41.136
Kinda. except Massi's already in jail.

849
00:36:41.236 --> 00:36:42.600
and everyone from his organization

850
00:36:42.699 --> 00:36:44.363
is either with him or dead.

851
00:36:44.463 --> 00:36:45.892
- So who'd want revenge? - Well. we need to

852
00:36:46.024 --> 00:36:47.389
figure that out. and fast.

853
00:36:47.521 --> 00:36:48.785
Because if this is about payback.

854
00:36:48.885 --> 00:36:51.380
Knight could be next on the list.

855
00:37:02.154 --> 00:37:04.250
I didn't want to wake you.

856
00:37:07.009 --> 00:37:08.606
How long have you been here?

857
00:37:08.706 --> 00:37:11.300
Just a few hours. I wanted to...

858
00:37:11.366 --> 00:37:13.660
be here when Ryan woke up.

859
00:37:13.760 --> 00:37:15.191
That's sweet.

860
00:37:15.324 --> 00:37:17.286
It's not. actually.

861
00:37:17.352 --> 00:37:19.580
Turns out he's been playing both of us.

862
00:37:19.646 --> 00:37:21.143
And I want answers.

863
00:37:21.243 --> 00:37:24.102
Played us? How?

864
00:37:24.203 --> 00:37:26.265
Ryan's charity is a front

865
00:37:26.365 --> 00:37:28.293
for a major drug ring.

866
00:37:28.393 --> 00:37:30.289
That's why he killed his friend.

867
00:37:30.421 --> 00:37:32.217
No.

868
00:37:32.284 --> 00:37:34.479
Can't be.

869
00:37:35.543 --> 00:37:37.339
I'm afraid so.

870
00:37:37.439 --> 00:37:39.833
The man that we thought we knew...

871
00:37:41.030 --> 00:37:42.527
...he's a lie.

872
00:37:42.626 --> 00:37:44.655
Special Agent Knight.

873
00:37:48.080 --> 00:37:50.641
Malone. You here to gloat?

874
00:37:50.740 --> 00:37:52.902
Actually. I'm here for your bag.

875
00:37:53.002 --> 00:37:55.098
You come for my job and my agency.

876
00:37:55.230 --> 00:37:56.660
Now you want my bag?

877
00:37:56.759 --> 00:38:00.817
I'm not giving you anything without a search warrant.

878
00:38:05.374 --> 00:38:07.601
Wow. That is a lot of trouble

879
00:38:07.701 --> 00:38:09.663
for a sweatpants and a bottle of water.

880
00:38:09.729 --> 00:38:11.891
The bag.

881
00:38:23.033 --> 00:38:24.860
Agent Knight.

882
00:38:24.994 --> 00:38:27.056
I can't believe it.

883
00:38:27.953 --> 00:38:29.682
Me either.

884
00:38:29.782 --> 00:38:31.047
This actually worked.

885
00:38:31.147 --> 00:38:34.140
I told you. She wouldn't be able to stop herself.

886
00:38:35.270 --> 00:38:36.966
What the hell are you talking about?

887
00:38:37.066 --> 00:38:38.728
This is a sting. Amanda.

888
00:38:38.828 --> 00:38:40.457
We played you.

889
00:38:40.557 --> 00:38:42.221
just like you played Ryan.

890
00:38:42.320 --> 00:38:44.482
There's cameras all down this hallway.

891
00:38:44.615 --> 00:38:46.211
You slipped the drugs into Knight's bag

892
00:38:46.278 --> 00:38:48.107
when she was. uh. sleeping.

893
00:38:48.207 --> 00:38:49.802
The final piece of your revenge.

894
00:38:49.902 --> 00:38:51.931
and this piece just fell right into your lap.

895
00:38:52.031 --> 00:38:54.524
Revenge? For what?

896
00:38:54.624 --> 00:38:58.084
You're Roland Massi's daughter.

897
00:38:59.513 --> 00:39:00.944
So what?

898
00:39:01.044 --> 00:39:02.705
He's rotting away in prison.

899
00:39:02.805 --> 00:39:04.336
I'm trying to move on.

900
00:39:04.435 --> 00:39:06.231
That must have been hard.

901
00:39:06.331 --> 00:39:08.991
Doors slamming in your face because of the Massi name.

902
00:39:09.058 --> 00:39:11.020
So. you changed your name.

903
00:39:11.120 --> 00:39:12.483
your look.

904
00:39:12.549 --> 00:39:14.179
tried to start a new life.

905
00:39:14.246 --> 00:39:15.742
But that wasn't enough. because the man

906
00:39:15.875 --> 00:39:17.704
who destroyed your family was still alive.

907
00:39:17.837 --> 00:39:20.232
And that's when you went looking for Harper.

908
00:39:20.364 --> 00:39:23.025
Got him to fall for you. to trust you.

909
00:39:23.125 --> 00:39:24.322
then you set him up.

910
00:39:24.422 --> 00:39:27.681
Drugs. murder. It almost worked.

911
00:39:27.813 --> 00:39:30.806
Until he barricaded himself in a warehouse

912
00:39:30.874 --> 00:39:32.503
and made one request.

913
00:39:32.602 --> 00:39:34.631
He called me.

914
00:39:34.730 --> 00:39:38.322
And now you'll serve 50 to life.

915
00:39:40.384 --> 00:39:42.213
Just like dad.

916
00:40:08.419 --> 00:40:10.016
Jess?

917
00:40:10.914 --> 00:40:12.609
I'm here.

918
00:40:22.386 --> 00:40:24.481
Well. welcome back. We've missed you.

919
00:40:24.548 --> 00:40:26.543
I've only been gone for a day.

920
00:40:26.676 --> 00:40:29.004
Well. it felt like a day and a half.

921
00:40:29.737 --> 00:40:32.064
Security clearance been reinstated.

922
00:40:32.164 --> 00:40:35.488
We got Amanda on everything.

923
00:40:35.555 --> 00:40:37.684
Murder. spiking Harper's protein shake with cocaine. all of it.

924
00:40:37.784 --> 00:40:40.744
I'm surprised you got Malone on our side.

925
00:40:40.844 --> 00:40:42.472
He was ready to hang me out to dry.

926
00:40:42.572 --> 00:40:44.136
Well. you should have seen his face

927
00:40:44.235 --> 00:40:47.594
when we told him that Amanda was Massi's daughter.

928
00:40:49.157 --> 00:40:52.783
Well. I guess the important part is that Harper's cleared.

929
00:40:52.849 --> 00:40:54.911
- recovering. - And hey.

930
00:40:55.010 --> 00:40:57.837
he turned his life around because of you.

931
00:40:57.970 --> 00:41:00.497
I guess I shouldn't have doubted myself.

932
00:41:00.597 --> 00:41:03.291
That's okay. We never did.

933
00:41:04.455 --> 00:41:05.552
Oh.

934
00:41:05.653 --> 00:41:08.013
Speaking of. uh. second chances...

935
00:41:09.610 --> 00:41:12.669
Agent Knight. Quick word?

936
00:41:16.992 --> 00:41:19.985
They're not thrilled to see me.

937
00:41:20.085 --> 00:41:21.848
They know we're friends now. right?

938
00:41:21.915 --> 00:41:24.142
Is that what we are?

939
00:41:25.572 --> 00:41:27.501
I'm here to clear the deck.

940
00:41:27.568 --> 00:41:30.561
I got a reputation as a hard-charger.

941
00:41:30.660 --> 00:41:32.590
but I own my mistakes.

942
00:41:32.722 --> 00:41:36.281
I misread some things. That's on me.

943
00:41:37.145 --> 00:41:38.508
You're forgiven.

944
00:41:38.609 --> 00:41:40.870
I wasn't asking for forgiveness.

945
00:41:42.100 --> 00:41:45.392
But I guess sometimes we forget.

946
00:41:45.492 --> 00:41:49.283
This job's not just about kicking down doors.

947
00:41:49.350 --> 00:41:51.579
It's about lifting people up.

948
00:41:52.443 --> 00:41:53.840
Yeah. it is.

949
00:41:55.801 --> 00:41:58.794
Oh. we don't validate parking. so...

950
00:42:02.286 --> 00:42:03.551
I couldn't resist.

951
00:42:03.650 --> 00:42:05.613
It's got my personal cell on the back.

952
00:42:05.678 --> 00:42:07.773
Are you hoping for a date?

953
00:42:07.840 --> 00:42:09.736
Uh. no. ma'am.

954
00:42:09.836 --> 00:42:12.362
I'm hoping for a job.

955
00:42:13.594 --> 00:42:15.822
I'm sure you've heard the rumors.

956
00:42:16.620 --> 00:42:18.815
I'll put in a good word for you.

957
00:42:23.071 --> 00:42:26.097
Captioning sponsored by CBS

958
00:42:26.197 --> 00:42:28.858
and TOYOTA.

959
00:42:28.958 --> 00:42:32.382
Captioned by Media Access Group at WGBH access.wgbh.org
